204	# iOS Setup (`ios.py`)
205	
206	## Tested on
207	
208	- iPhone X running iOS 16.7.12
209	- palera1n rootless jailbreak
210	- Frida 17.6.0
211	- Custom Python 3.12.5 build (see below)
212	- Gemini CLI v0.33.1 (Gemini 2.5 / Gemini 3)
213	
214	## Prerequisites
215	
216	- A jailbroken iOS device (rootless jailbreak, e.g. palera1n)
217	- SSH access to the device
218	- A Frida server running on-device (match the frida-python version)
219	
220	## Installing Python 3.12
221	
222	No modern Python runtime exists in the Procursus repo for rootless jailbreaks. A custom Python 3.12.5 `.deb` is provided in `ios_precompiled/`. This is based on [python3.12-ios-arm64](https://github.com/k1tty-xz/python3.12-ios-arm64) by k1tty-xz, modified for rootless jailbreak support (`/var/jb/` layout).
223	
224	```bash
225	# Copy the deb to the device
226	scp ios_precompiled/python3.12_3.12.5-1_iphoneos-arm64.deb mobile@<IPHONE_IP>:/tmp/
227	
228	# Install (dpkg needs root — use sudo)
229	ssh mobile@<IPHONE_IP>
230	sudo dpkg -i /tmp/python3.12_3.12.5-1_iphoneos-arm64.deb
231	
232	# Verify
233	python3 --version
234	```
235	
236	This installs to `/var/jb/usr/local/` (rootless jailbreak layout). It includes `libpython3.12.dylib`, the standard library, and OpenSSL/libffi support.
237	
238	## Installing pip
239	
240	```bash
241	python3 -m ensurepip
242	python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
243	```
244	
245	## Installing precompiled wheels
246	
247	All required native wheels are provided in `ios_precompiled/`. These were cross-compiled from macOS targeting `arm64-apple-ios`.
248	
249	```bash
250	# Copy all wheels to the device
251	scp ios_precompiled/*.whl mobile@<IPHONE_IP>:/tmp/
252	
253	# Install each wheel (order matters for dependencies)
254	ssh mobile@<IPHONE_IP>
255	
256	python3 -m pip install /tmp/cffi-*.whl
257	python3 -m pip install /tmp/cryptography-*.whl
258	python3 -m pip install /tmp/pydantic_core-*.whl
259	python3 -m pip install /tmp/rpds_py-*.whl
260	python3 -m pip install /tmp/PyYAML-*.whl
261	python3 -m pip install /tmp/frida-*.whl
262	python3 -m pip install /tmp/lupa-*.whl
263	```
264	
265	### Signing after install (required)
266	
267	iOS requires code signing for all native extensions. After every `pip install` of a wheel containing `.so` files, you must re-sign them with `ldid`:
268	
269	```bash
270	PY_SITE="/var/jb/var/mobile/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages"
271	
272	# Sign all native extensions
273	find "$PY_SITE" -name "*.so" -type f -exec ldid -S {} \;
274	
275	# Or sign a specific package after install
276	find "$PY_SITE/cryptography" -name "*.so" -type f -exec ldid -S {} \;
277	```
278	
279	If you skip this step, Python will crash with `Killed: 9` when importing any native module.
280	
281	## Installing pure-Python dependencies
282	
283	These don't need signing since they have no native code:
284	
285	```bash
286	python3 -m pip install -r requirements-ios.txt
287	```
288	
289	**WARNING**: Do not run `pip install frida` — it will try to download a prebuilt binary that won't work. Use the provided wheel instead.
290	
291	**WARNING**: FastMCP 3.x has breaking API changes. This repo is still on FastMCP 2.x for both Android and iOS — migration hasn’t kept pace with upstream. Use `requirements-ios.txt`; don’t install an unpinned `fastmcp`.
292	
293	## Fixing frida-tools shebangs (important)
294	
295	When you install `frida-tools` (which provides `frida-compile`), the script shebangs default to the Procursus Python 3.9 path. You need to update them to point to your Python 3.12:
296	
297	```bash
298	# Install frida-tools over the base frida library
299	python3 -m pip install frida-tools
300	
301	# Fix shebangs in frida-tools scripts
302	SCRIPTS="/var/jb/var/mobile/.local/bin"
303	for script in "$SCRIPTS/frida" "$SCRIPTS/frida-compile" "$SCRIPTS/frida-discover" \
304	              "$SCRIPTS/frida-kill" "$SCRIPTS/frida-ls-devices" "$SCRIPTS/frida-ps" \
305	              "$SCRIPTS/frida-trace"; do
306	    if [ -f "$script" ]; then
307	        sed -i '' '1s|.*|#!/var/jb/usr/local/bin/python3|' "$script"
308	    fi
309	done
310	
311	# Verify
312	head -1 "$SCRIPTS/frida-compile"
313	# Should show: #!/var/jb/usr/local/bin/python3
314	```
315	
316	Without this fix, `frida-compile` will either fail to launch or use the wrong Python and miss all your installed packages.
317	
318	## Installing node_modules for frida-compile (no Node.js required on-device)
319	
320	This is a nodeless setup — Node.js does **not** need to be installed on the iPhone. However, `frida-compile` still resolves bridge imports from a `node_modules/` directory at runtime. Since `frida-objc-bridge` is just a JavaScript wrapper (no native code), you can install it on any machine with Node.js and copy the result over:
321	
322	```bash
323	# On your Mac/PC (or any machine with npm):
324	mkdir /tmp/ios_modules && cd /tmp/ios_modules
325	npm install frida-objc-bridge
326	
327	# Copy to iPhone:
328	scp -r /tmp/ios_modules/node_modules mobile@<IPHONE_IP>:~/
329	```
330	
331	The `node_modules/` folder just needs to be in the same directory where `ios.py` runs (the home directory).
332	
333	## Running the server
334	
335	```bash
336	# Place ios.py in your home directory
337	scp ios.py mobile@<IPHONE_IP>:~/
338	
339	# Run as the mobile user
340	ssh mobile@<IPHONE_IP>
341	cd ~
342	python3 ios.py
343	```
344	
345	The server starts on `0.0.0.0:6767` with streamable HTTP transport.
346	
347	## Compiled packages reference
348	
349	All precompiled packages in `ios_precompiled/`:
350	
351	| Package | Version | Why it's needed |
352	|---------|---------|----------------|
353	| **Python 3.12.5** (`.deb`) | 3.12.5-1 | Base runtime — not available via Procursus for rootless jailbreaks |
354	| **frida-python** | 17.6.0 | Core Frida bindings |
355	| **pydantic-core** | 2.41.5 | Required by FastMCP / pydantic |
356	| **cryptography** | 47.0.0.dev1 | Dependency chain for FastMCP; needed SIGILL fix for A11 (iPhone X) |
357	| **cffi** | 2.0.1.dev0 | Required by cryptography |
358	| **pyyaml** | 7.0.0.dev0 | Required by FastMCP deps |
359	| **rpds-py** | 0.30.0 | Required by FastMCP deps |
360	| **lupa** | 2.6 | Lua embedding |
361	
362	## Target application notes
363	
364	As a PoC we use [DVIA-v2](https://github.com/prateek147/DVIA-v2) for jailbreak detection bypass.
365	
366	**NOTE**: DVIA-v2's jailbreak detection ("Jailbreak Test 2") does not reliably detect rootless jailbreaks (e.g. palera1n) because it checks for files/paths that only exist on rootful setups. To make the demo work, you need to patch the app so the jailbreak check always returns `true` (i.e. "Device is jailbroken") — then use Frida to bypass it back to `false`. This is similar to the Android setup where AndroGoat's `isRooted1` logic needed uncommenting to detect Magisk's non-standard `su` path.
367	
368	## iOS Happy Path
369	
370	Full workflow validated with Gemini CLI v0.33.1 (Gemini 2.5 / Gemini 3):
371	
372	1. Agent opens target app (e.g. DVIA-v2)
373	2. Agent creates interactive session with the running process
374	3. Agent runs one-shot script to enumerate ObjC classes containing "jailbreak" — output returned inline
375	4. Agent creates persistent hook to bypass jailbreak detection — hooks stay active
376	5. User triggers the jailbreak check in-app, sees "Device is not jailbroken"
377	6. Agent calls `get_session_messages` and sees hook intercept logs
378	
379	```
